From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arsslen Idadi <arsslens021@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:29:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] tests/dbusmock/fprintd: Report an enrolled finger on
 scripted identification

A scripted verify-match on a device that identifies (VerifyStart with
"any") reached emit_verify_status() with no matched finger, so it raised
"Unknown finger name 'None'" instead of reporting an enrolled finger, as
SetVerifyScript's documentation says it does.

(cherry picked from commit c9cf263d408be3d954c84d7c07521ac80e2ebe48)
---
 tests/dbusmock/fprintd.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/dbusmock/fprintd.py b/tests/dbusmock/fprintd.py
index 80436c3..6d0eb51 100644
--- a/tests/dbusmock/fprintd.py
+++ b/tests/dbusmock/fprintd.py
@@ -225,7 +225,7 @@ def glib_sleep(timeout):
 def emit_verify_status(device, result, done, matched_finger=None):
     if device.selected_finger in VALID_FINGER_NAMES:
         matched_finger = device.selected_finger
-    elif matched_finger == 'any':
+    elif matched_finger in (None, 'any'):
         enrolled = device.fingers.get(device.claimed_user) or []
         if enrolled:
             matched_finger = enrolled[0]
